        <mxCell id="gpu-server__port_top_6810_3050" value="&lt;span style=&quot;font-variant-ligatures:none&quot;&gt;TCP 443&lt;/span&gt;" style="rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=6;html=1;fillColor=#64748b;strokeColor=#f8fafc;strokeWidth=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;fontStyle=1;fontFamily=JetBrains Mono,Noto Sans Mono,DejaVu Sans Mono,monospace;fontSize=9;fontColor=#ffffff;movable=0;resizable=0;" vertex="1" parent="gpu-server">
          <mxGeometry x="307.10000000000036" y="-8" width="45.8" height="16" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="card-steps" value="&lt;span style=&quot;font-variant-ligatures:none&quot;&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#059669&quot;&gt;●&lt;/font&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;b&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#0f172a&quot; style=&quot;font-size:13px&quot;&gt;Request path · a user asks an agent that runs code, calls a model and a tool&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;line-height:1.6&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color:#0f172a;color:#ffffff;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 4px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;1&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&quot;background-color:#0f172a;color:#ffffff;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 4px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;2&lt;/span&gt; The user signs in to Keycloak and asks the agent, sending a user token. &lt;span style=&quot;background-color:#0f172a;color:#ffffff;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 4px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;3&lt;/span&gt; The agent exchanges it for its own short token (or uses client_credentials when it acts alone).&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color:#0f172a;color:#ffffff;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 4px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;4&lt;/span&gt; The agent creates a SandboxClaim; the controller hands it a warm sandbox from the pool of the chosen tier. &lt;span style=&quot;background-color:#0f172a;color:#ffffff;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 4px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;5&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&quot;background-color:#0f172a;color:#ffffff;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 4px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;6&lt;/span&gt; It sends commands through the sandbox router, which forwards them to the sandbox pod (gVisor here; Kata the same way).&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color:#0f172a;color:#ffffff;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 4px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;7&lt;/span&gt; The agent asks a model at the AI gateway&amp;#39;s internal listener; JWT and CEL checks run, then &lt;span style=&quot;background-color:#0f172a;color:#ffffff;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 4px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;8&lt;/span&gt; the rate limit service checks the agent&amp;#39;s daily token budget.&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color:#0f172a;color:#ffffff;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 4px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;9&lt;/span&gt; The LLM proxy sends the request to Gemini; &lt;span style=&quot;background-color:#0f172a;color:#ffffff;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 4px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;10&lt;/span&gt; after a 429 the failover policy sends it to the GPU server.&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color:#0f172a;color:#ffffff;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 4px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;11&lt;/span&gt;–&lt;span style=&quot;background-color:#0f172a;color:#ffffff;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 4px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;13&lt;/span&gt; A tool call on /mcp goes through the MCP proxy of the gateway to the ToolHive proxy, then to the MCP server over JSON-RPC.&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color:#0f172a;color:#ffffff;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 4px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;14&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&quot;background-color:#0f172a;color:#ffffff;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 4px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;15&lt;/span&gt; The gateway exports GenAI spans to Alloy, which scrapes its metrics and writes traces to Tempo and metrics to VictoriaMetrics.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/span&gt;" style="rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=16;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#e2e8f0;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=20;spacingTop=14;spacingRight=16;fontFamily=JetBrains Mono,Noto Sans Mono,DejaVu Sans Mono,monospace;fontSize=11;fontColor=#1e293b;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="5840" width="3600" height="320" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="card-background" value="&lt;span style=&quot;font-variant-ligatures:none&quot;&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#d97706&quot;&gt;●&lt;/font&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;b&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#0f172a&quot; style=&quot;font-size:13px&quot;&gt;Background · what is set up before the request&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;line-height:1.6&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;border:1px solid #0f172a;color:#0f172a;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 3px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;A&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&quot;border:1px solid #0f172a;color:#0f172a;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 3px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;B&lt;/span&gt; When a project gets an agent, the CMP creates its Keycloak client and writes the client secret to Vault.&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;border:1px solid #0f172a;color:#0f172a;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 3px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;C&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&quot;border:1px solid #0f172a;color:#0f172a;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 3px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;D&lt;/span&gt; The secrets operator reads it and writes the Kubernetes Secret mounted by the agent.&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;border:1px solid #0f172a;color:#0f172a;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 3px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;E&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&quot;border:1px solid #0f172a;color:#0f172a;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 3px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;F&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&quot;border:1px solid #0f172a;color:#0f172a;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 3px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;G&lt;/span&gt; The agentgateway controller, the sandbox controller and the ToolHive operator watch their CRDs and configure the proxy or write what they generate (pods, services).&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;border:1px solid #0f172a;color:#0f172a;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 3px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;H&lt;/span&gt; Argo CD applies everything from Git, the AI landing zone included.&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;border:1px solid #0f172a;color:#0f172a;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 3px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;I&lt;/span&gt; The GPU server sits on the same local network as the cluster; Cilium lets the gateway reach its /32 over HTTPS and nothing else.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/span&gt;" style="rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=16;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#e2e8f0;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=20;spacingTop=14;spacingRight=16;fontFamily=JetBrains Mono,Noto Sans Mono,DejaVu Sans Mono,monospace;fontSize=11;fontColor=#1e293b;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="3700" y="5840" width="3600" height="320" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
